   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": null
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-799435",
   "speaker": "Penny Wong",
   "party": "Labor",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-03-15",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The senator moved that the bills be taken together and proceed without formalities, and they were read a first time."
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-799436",
   "speaker": "Penny Wong",
   "party": "Labor",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-03-15",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Healthcare Identifiers Bill 2010 and related bill were introduced to establish a single national identifier system for patients, healthcare providers and organisations, aiming to support e-health records and improve safety by ensuring accurate, consistent identification. The Offshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Legislation Amendment Bill 2010 makes changes including redirecting registration fees to establish a National Offshore Petroleum Regulator by 2012 and expanding the National Offshore Petroleum Safety Authority’s functions to cover non-occupational health and safety aspects of structural integrity."
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-801608",
   "speaker": null,
   "party": null,
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-06-24",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": null
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-801609",
   "speaker": "Nicola Roxon",
   "party": "Labor",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-06-24",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": null
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-801742",
   "speaker": null,
   "party": null,
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-06-24",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": null
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-801743",
   "speaker": "Concetta Fierravanti-Wells",
   "party": "Liberal",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-06-24",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The speaker argued that the government mismanaged the Healthcare Identifiers Bill, blaming Minister Roxon for rushed legislation and lack of consultation, while supporting e-health and noting the coalition’s eight proposed amendments, six of which were accepted. The coalition did not oppose the bill but rejected Greens amendments for an opt-out option."
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-801744",
   "speaker": null,
   "party": null,
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-06-24",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": null
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-801745",
   "speaker": "Joe Ludwig",
   "party": "Labor",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-06-24",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The government moved amendments to the Healthcare Identifiers Bill 2010, adding definitions for contracted service providers, healthcare provider organisations, and the Defence Department, and opposed Greens amendments allowing individuals to opt out of the identifier scheme, arguing this would create parallel systems and undermine the unique identifier. It also confirmed that withholding an individual health identifier does not preclude access to health services."
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-801750",
   "speaker": "Joe Ludwig",
   "party": "Labor",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-06-24",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The speaker moved government amendments to replace \"Privacy Commissioner\" with \"Information Commissioner\" in sections 29 and 30, and to set the commencement of Schedule 3 to follow the commencement of the Australian Information Commissioner Act 2010 and the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010. The amendments were agreed to."
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-801751",
   "speaker": "Joe Ludwig",
